{"agent":"bhp","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`research_id` is `nargs=\"?\"` on the shared research parser, and the show branch does `a.id = a.research_id or \"\"`. `ddflow research show` (no id) therefore does not fail at parse time; it calls `cmd_research_show` with an empty id. The same optional positional swallows stray tokens on the other verbs: `ddflow research list R1` and `ddflow research add R1 --question q --verdict THEORETICAL` used to be unrecognized arguments, and now succeed while ignoring `R1` (add never copies `research_id` onto the record). That also clobbers a parsed `--id`: `ddflow research show --id R1` sets `a.id` from the flag and then overwrites it with `\"\"`.","digest":"047d2c033d8ef9ab","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:338","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:338"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Research help text changed from `{add,list}` to `{add,list,show}` (and `test_research_add.py` asserts the new spelling), but the pinned CLI-help snapshot was not updated. A golden run that snapshots `research --help` fails on the unfixed amber file.","digest":"2129677e8d3365fc","family":"xai","location":"tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5336,"diff_sha":"b2bd3bd7f601cb10135682cfc2dee81266f9ab661810dc915dd26d16274a9029","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Bec642db4a9","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":37.8,"excluded_bytes":1671,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr"],"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"ff80e9c514